IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Rhode Island Works Program Rules and Regulations (218-RICR-20-00-2), Department of Human Services -- the seat-neutral
-- core, in the rule's own terms, for RI Works cash assistance (Rhode Island's TANF programme):
--   the eligible child (s 2.5.2); the resource limit and the vehicle exclusion (ss 2.14.1(A), 2.14.2(F));
--   countable income: the earned income disregard, the dependent care disregard, the earned income set aside and the
--   child support exclusion (ss 2.15.2, 2.15.3(D)-(E), 2.15.5);
--   the cash assistance standard by plan size and the subsidized housing reduction (ss 2.18.1, 2.18.2);
--   the payment, and the $10 minimum (ss 2.15.5(B), 2.18.3(A)(5), 2.18.5);
--   the 60-month time limit, its exceptions and the hardship extension (ss 2.6, 2.6.1, 2.6.3, 2.6.4);
--   the work penalty for a family of two (s 2.11.11(B));
--   duties with a deadline: reporting changes (s 2.21.2), the Interim Report (s 2.22.1), and the hearing request and
--   continued benefits (ss 2.11.12, 2.29.1, 2.29.3), as regulative rules.
--
-- Edition: the Part in force on 24 October 2026 (Technical Revision, effective 16 February 2025 to 10 November 2026),
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/218-ricr-20-00-2-2025-02-16.txt. The Amendment effective 10 November 2026 is
-- deposited beside it (218-ricr-20-00-2-2026-11-10.txt); the one rule it changes that is encoded here, the child support
-- exclusion, follows it for months from that date.
-- The enabling statute, R.I. Gen. Laws ch. 40-5.2, is not deposited (rilegislature.gov did not respond).
--
-- The seat questions are in ri-works-seat.l4. BASELINE ENCODING. Not advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Rhode Island Works Program Rules and Regulations (218-RICR-20-00-2)`

§§ `s 2.5.2 -- the eligible child`

-- s 2.5.2(A): "To be eligible for cash assistance, a parent (or other caretaker relative) must have a needy child:
-- 1. Under the age of eighteen (18); or, 2. Between eighteen (18) and nineteen (19) who meet the criteria established
-- within this Section." s 2.18.3(A)(1)(b): an eligible child aged 18 "if they are a full-time student in a secondary
-- school (or at the equivalent level of a GED program, vocational or technical training) and reasonably expected to
-- complete the program before or in the month of their nineteenth (19th) birthday."
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
      `is a full-time student in secondary school, a GED program or equivalent vocational or technical training` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is reasonably expected to finish before or in the month of their nineteenth birthday` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an eligible child by age` IF
        `age` LESS THAN 18
    OR  (    `age` AT LEAST 18
         AND `age` LESS THAN 19
         AND `is a full-time student in secondary school, a GED program or equivalent vocational or technical training`
         AND `is reasonably expected to finish before or in the month of their nineteenth birthday`)

§§ `s 2.14 -- resources`

-- s 2.14.1(A): "No family shall be eligible for cash assistance if the combined value of its available resources (reduced
-- by any obligations or debts with respect to such resources) exceed five thousand dollars ($5,000.00)."
`the resource limit` MEANS 5000

-- s 2.14.2(F)(1): "The following shall not be counted as resources of the family: a. One vehicle for each adult household
-- member but not to exceed two (2) vehicles per household". (F)(1)(b): vehicles used primarily to produce income are also
-- excluded (left out of the list by the person). s 2.14.2(F)... "(2) If the vehicle is not excluded, count the vehicle's
-- equity value (which is fair market value less encumbrances)". The rule does not say which vehicles are the excluded
-- ones; the person lists the equity of each vehicle with the ones they claim excluded first (NOTES.md finding 4).
GIVEN `number of adults in the household` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of vehicles excluded` `number of adults in the household` MEANS
    IF `number of adults in the household` GREATER THAN 2 THEN 2 ELSE `number of adults in the household`

GIVEN `how many to skip` IS A NUMBER
      `equities` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the equity counted` `how many to skip` `equities` MEANS
    CONSIDER `equities`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN e FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF `how many to skip` GREATER THAN 0
        THEN `the equity counted` (`how many to skip` MINUS 1) rest
        ELSE e PLUS `the equity counted` 0 rest

-- `other countable resources` is the equity value of every other non-excluded resource (cash, bank accounts, stocks and
-- bonds, real property other than the home, luxury items), net of debts against them (a fact).
GIVEN `other countable resources` IS A NUMBER
      `number of adults in the household` IS A NUMBER
      `vehicle equities, excluded ones first` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the countable resources` `other countable resources` `number of adults in the household` `vehicle equities, excluded ones first` MEANS
    `other countable resources` PLUS (`the equity counted` (`the number of vehicles excluded` `number of adults in the household`) `vehicle equities, excluded ones first`)

GIVEN `countable resources` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the resources are within the limit` IF
    `countable resources` AT MOST `the resource limit`

§§ `s 2.18 -- the cash assistance standard`

-- s 2.18.1, table "Cash Assistance Monthly Standard" by plan size: 1 $510; 2 $701; 3 $865; 4 $990; 5 $1115; 6 $1,240;
-- 7 $1,365; 8 $1,490; 9 $1,615; 10 $1,740; 11 $1,865; 12 $1,990; 13 $2,115; 14 $2,240; 15 $2,365; "Add for each person
-- over 15 $125.00". (The semi-monthly column for plan size 10 reads "$724.50870.00" in the version in force: NOTES.md
-- finding 9.)
GIVEN `plan size` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the monthly standard` `plan size` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `plan size` AT MOST 0  THEN 0
        IF `plan size` EQUALS 1   THEN 510
        IF `plan size` EQUALS 2   THEN 701
        IF `plan size` EQUALS 3   THEN 865
        IF `plan size` EQUALS 4   THEN 990
        IF `plan size` EQUALS 5   THEN 1115
        IF `plan size` EQUALS 6   THEN 1240
        IF `plan size` EQUALS 7   THEN 1365
        IF `plan size` EQUALS 8   THEN 1490
        IF `plan size` EQUALS 9   THEN 1615
        IF `plan size` EQUALS 10  THEN 1740
        IF `plan size` EQUALS 11  THEN 1865
        IF `plan size` EQUALS 12  THEN 1990
        IF `plan size` EQUALS 13  THEN 2115
        IF `plan size` EQUALS 14  THEN 2240
        IF `plan size` EQUALS 15  THEN 2365
        OTHERWISE 2365 PLUS (125 TIMES (`plan size` MINUS 15))

-- s 2.18.2(A): "For any family residing in subsidized housing, the RI Works payment standard is reduced by sixty-five
-- dollars ($65.00)". "Subsidized housing" means "housing for a family whose rent is restricted to a percentage of its
-- income" (s 2.2).
GIVEN `plan size` IS A NUMBER
      `lives in subsidized housing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the payment standard` `plan size` `lives in subsidized housing` MEANS
    IF `lives in subsidized housing`
    THEN `the monthly standard` `plan size` MINUS 65
    ELSE `the monthly standard` `plan size`

§§ `s 2.15 -- countable income`

-- s 2.15.5(B)(1)(a): "Disregard all the monthly earned income of each dependent child". (b): "Disregard five hundred
-- twenty-five dollars ($525.00) plus one half (1/2) of the earned income not already disregarded ... This disregard is
-- allowed for each individual who has otherwise been found eligible to receive cash assistance."
-- s 2.15.3(E), the earned income set aside: the earned income of an adult "who gains employment while an active RI Works
-- household member" is, "As requested by an adult household member", excluded "for the first (1st) six (6) months of
-- employment ... or until the household's total gross income exceeds one hundred eighty-five percent (185%) of the Federal
-- Poverty Level" (a fact: whether it applies this month).
GIVEN `gross monthly earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the earned income set aside applies this month` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`earnings remaining after the earned income disregard` `gross monthly earnings` `the earned income set aside applies this month` MEANS
    IF `the earned income set aside applies this month` OR `gross monthly earnings` AT MOST 525
    THEN 0
    ELSE (`gross monthly earnings` MINUS 525) TIMES 50%

-- s 2.15.5(B)(2): "Disregard the actual amount of the expense paid in a calendar month ... for each dependent child or
-- incapacitated adult living in the home and receiving cash assistance. b. This disregard may not exceed one hundred
-- seventy-five dollars ($175.00) per month per child age two (2) and older or an incapacitated adult. For a child under the
-- age of two (2), this disregard may not exceed two hundred dollars ($200.00) per month."
GIVEN `care paid for children under two` IS A NUMBER
      `children under two in paid care` IS A NUMBER
      `care paid for children two and over and incapacitated adults` IS A NUMBER
      `children two and over and incapacitated adults in paid care` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the dependent care disregard` `care paid for children under two` `children under two in paid care` `care paid for children two and over and incapacitated adults` `children two and over and incapacitated adults in paid care` MEANS
    LET `cap under two` MEANS 200 TIMES `children under two in paid care`
        `cap two and over` MEANS 175 TIMES `children two and over and incapacitated adults in paid care`
        `under two allowed` MEANS IF `care paid for children under two` LESS THAN `cap under two` THEN `care paid for children under two` ELSE `cap under two`
        `two and over allowed` MEANS IF `care paid for children two and over and incapacitated adults` LESS THAN `cap two and over` THEN `care paid for children two and over and incapacitated adults` ELSE `cap two and over`
    IN `under two allowed` PLUS `two and over allowed`

-- s 2.15.3(D)(1) (version in force to 10 November 2026): "The first (1st) fifty dollars ($50.00) of the child support
-- payment paid in any month by a non-custodial parent ..., or the actual amount ... if ... less than fifty dollars
-- ($50.00), shall be paid to the family ... and is excluded from the family's income." The Amendment effective
-- 10 November 2026: "The first one hundred dollars ($100.00) for one (1) child, or two hundred dollars ($200.00) for two
-- (2) or more children". In both, only one such amount for the family however many non-custodial parents pay.
GIVEN `the month` IS A DATE
      `children the support is paid for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the child support exclusion limit` `the month` `children the support is paid for` MEANS
    IF `the month` LESS THAN (Date 10 11 2026)
    THEN 50
    ELSE IF `children the support is paid for` AT LEAST 2
         THEN 200
         ELSE 100

GIVEN `the month` IS A DATE
      `child support paid this month` IS A NUMBER
      `children the support is paid for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the child support counted` `the month` `child support paid this month` `children the support is paid for` MEANS
    LET `limit` MEANS `the child support exclusion limit` `the month` `children the support is paid for`
    IN IF `child support paid this month` GREATER THAN `limit` THEN `child support paid this month` MINUS `limit` ELSE 0

-- s 2.15.5(A): "net adjusted income equals the total of any unearned income plus any amount remaining from earned income
-- after deducting the earned income disregards and any allowable dependent care disregards." The dependent care
-- disregard comes off what is left of earnings and cannot take it below nil (NOTES.md finding 6).
GIVEN `earnings remaining` IS A NUMBER
      `dependent care disregard` IS A NUMBER
      `unearned income counted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the net adjusted income` `earnings remaining` `dependent care disregard` `unearned income counted` MEANS
    LET `earned after care` MEANS IF `earnings remaining` GREATER THAN `dependent care disregard` THEN `earnings remaining` MINUS `dependent care disregard` ELSE 0
    IN `earned after care` PLUS `unearned income counted`

§§ `ss 2.15.5(B), 2.18.3, 2.18.5 -- eligibility and the payment`

-- s 2.15.5(B): net adjusted income "must be less than the appropriate cash assistance standard in order for financial
-- eligibility to exist." s 2.18.3(A)(5): "the cash assistance standard corresponding to the plan size ... (minus any
-- available income) is the basis of the cash assistance grant." s 2.18.5(A): "no payment of cash assistance shall be made
-- for any month if the amount of such payment would be less than ten dollars ($10.00)"; (B)(2): a family denied payment
-- solely for this is a recipient "for all other purposes".
DECLARE `Monthly cash assistance` IS ONE OF
    `not financially eligible: net adjusted income is not less than the payment standard (s 2.15.5(B))`
    `eligible, but no payment this month: the amount would be less than $10 (s 2.18.5); still a recipient for all other purposes`
    `a monthly payment of` HAS `the amount` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `payment standard` IS A NUMBER
      `net adjusted income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Monthly cash assistance`
`the monthly cash assistance` `payment standard` `net adjusted income` MEANS
    IF `net adjusted income` AT LEAST `payment standard`
    THEN `not financially eligible: net adjusted income is not less than the payment standard (s 2.15.5(B))`
    ELSE IF (`payment standard` MINUS `net adjusted income`) LESS THAN 10
         THEN `eligible, but no payment this month: the amount would be less than $10 (s 2.18.5); still a recipient for all other purposes`
         ELSE `a monthly payment of` (`payment standard` MINUS `net adjusted income`)

§§ `s 2.6 -- the time limit`

-- s 2.6(A): "a maximum lifetime limit of sixty (60) months of cash receipt, since May 1, 1997", counting family cash
-- assistance from other states (s 2.6(D)) and months under sanction, but not months as a minor dependent child
-- (s 2.6(D)(2)). s 2.6.1(A): "The time limit shall not apply in the instances of (1) a minor child(ren) living with a
-- single parent who receives SSI benefits, or with two-parents who both receive SSI benefits, and (2) a minor child(ren)
-- living with a legally responsible non-parent caretaker relative who is not in the cash assistance payment."
-- s 2.6.3(A): a hardship extension "may be granted" if all other requirements are met and one of five criteria applies;
-- s 2.6.4(A): "an initial hardship extension for six (6) months. Additional six (6) month hardships are available."
-- Whether DHS grants it is DHS's (a fact).
DECLARE `Time limit position` IS ONE OF
    `the time limit does not apply to this family (s 2.6.1)`
    `within the time limit` HAS `months remaining` IS A NUMBER
    `the 60-month limit is reached, but a hardship extension of six months at a time is granted (ss 2.6.3, 2.6.4)`
    `the 60-month limit is reached; cash assistance ends unless DHS grants a hardship extension, for which one of the s 2.6.3 criteria is needed`

GIVEN `months of cash assistance counted` IS A NUMBER
      `the children live with a single parent on SSI, or two parents both on SSI` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the children live with a non-parent caretaker relative who is not in the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `DHS has granted a hardship extension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Time limit position`
`the time limit position` `months of cash assistance counted` `the children live with a single parent on SSI, or two parents both on SSI` `the children live with a non-parent caretaker relative who is not in the payment` `DHS has granted a hardship extension` MEANS
    IF `the children live with a single parent on SSI, or two parents both on SSI` OR `the children live with a non-parent caretaker relative who is not in the payment`
    THEN `the time limit does not apply to this family (s 2.6.1)`
    ELSE IF `months of cash assistance counted` LESS THAN 60
         THEN `within the time limit` (60 MINUS `months of cash assistance counted`)
         ELSE IF `DHS has granted a hardship extension`
              THEN `the 60-month limit is reached, but a hardship extension of six months at a time is granted (ss 2.6.3, 2.6.4)`
              ELSE `the 60-month limit is reached; cash assistance ends unless DHS grants a hardship extension, for which one of the s 2.6.3 criteria is needed`

-- s 2.6.3(A)(1)-(5): the criteria (each a fact; (5) needs a DHS supervisor's approval).
GIVEN `has a documented significant incapacity, a pending SSI or SSDI application, and is in an ORS plan or has applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `cares full time for a significantly disabled family member at home` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is homeless` IS A BOOLEAN
      `cannot pursue employment because of current documented domestic violence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `cannot work because of a critical other condition a DHS supervisor approves` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets a hardship extension criterion` IF
        `has a documented significant incapacity, a pending SSI or SSDI application, and is in an ORS plan or has applied`
    OR  `cares full time for a significantly disabled family member at home`
    OR  `is homeless`
    OR  `cannot pursue employment because of current documented domestic violence`
    OR  `cannot work because of a critical other condition a DHS supervisor approves`

§§ `s 2.11.11 -- the work penalty`

-- s 2.11.11(A): "The amount of cash assistance ... shall be reduced by the portion of the family's benefit attributable to
-- any parent who, without good cause, has failed to enter into an individual employment plan or has failed to comply".
-- (B): "For a family size of two (2), the benefit reduction ... shall be computed utilizing a family size of three (3), in
-- which the parent's portion equals one hundred five dollars ($105.00)." For other family sizes the rule does not say how
-- the parent's portion is found, so it is an input (NOTES.md finding 10).
GIVEN `family size` IS A NUMBER
      `the parent's portion, as DHS computes it` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the work penalty reduction` `family size` `the parent's portion, as DHS computes it` MEANS
    IF `family size` EQUALS 2 THEN 105 ELSE `the parent's portion, as DHS computes it`

§§ `ss 2.21, 2.22, 2.11.12, 2.29 -- duties with a deadline (regulative)`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the adult family member`
    `the household`
    `the recipient`
    `the Department`

DECLARE `Act` IS ONE OF
    `report the change`
    `report the absence of the minor child`
    `return the completed Interim Report with its verifications`
    `request a hearing`
    `request a hearing and continued benefits`
    `mail a notice of adverse action`

-- s 2.21.2(A): adult family members must "report any changes in income, resources, family composition, or other factors
-- which can affect eligibility or payment level, within ten (10) days of the change in circumstances", except
-- (A)(1): the temporary absence of a minor child for thirty or more consecutive days, to be reported "by the end of the
-- five (5) day period that begins with the date that the adult family member(s) becomes aware". (B) lists the ten-day
-- changes. Days run from the change (or from becoming aware, for the absence).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the duty to report a change` MEANS
    PARTY `the adult family member`
    MUST  `report the change`
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the adult family member` BECAUSE "a change was not reported within ten days (s 2.21.2); no supplementary benefits for an unreported increase (s 2.21.6(A)), and an overpayment is recovered (s 2.21.6(B))"

-- The five-day period "begins with the date" of becoming aware, so that day is day 1 and the last day is day 5: WITHIN 4
-- from that day (NOTES.md finding 12).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the duty to report a child's absence` MEANS
    PARTY `the adult family member`
    MUST  `report the absence of the minor child`
    WITHIN 4
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the adult family member` BECAUSE "the absence of a minor child for 30 or more days was not reported within the five-day period (s 2.21.2(A)(1))"

-- s 2.22.1(A): households "must complete the form in its entirety and mail the form along with the required verifications
-- back to the Department by the fifth (5th) day of the sixth (6th) month of certification." (B): "Failure to return the
-- Interim Report form will result in closure". s 2.22.2(B): if it is late, DHS "must send a warning notice", and the
-- household "will have ten (10) days from the date of mailing to return" it, "or the case will auto-close by the end of the
-- sixth (6th) month". Days run from the first day of the sixth month: the 5th is day 4.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the duty to return the Interim Report` MEANS
    PARTY `the household`
    MUST  `return the completed Interim Report with its verifications`
    WITHIN 4
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the household` BECAUSE "the Interim Report was not returned by the fifth day of the sixth month of certification; DHS must send a warning notice (s 2.22.2(B))"

-- After the warning notice: ten days from its mailing.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the duty to return the Interim Report after a warning notice` MEANS
    PARTY `the household`
    MUST  `return the completed Interim Report with its verifications`
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the household` BECAUSE "the Interim Report was not returned within ten days of the warning notice; the case auto-closes by the end of the sixth month (s 2.22.2(B))"

-- s 2.29.1(B): "the recipient must be notified by issuing a notice of adverse action at least ten days prior to the
-- effective date." For the person: the earliest day a reduction, suspension or ending can take effect.
GIVEN `the day the notice is mailed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earliest effective date of an adverse action` `the day the notice is mailed` MEANS
    `the day the notice is mailed` PLUS 10

-- s 2.11.12(A): "they may request a hearing before the DHS Hearing Officer within thirty (30) days of the mailing of the
-- notice of adverse action. The individual may request that benefits be continued pending the outcome of the hearing if the
-- request is made within ten (10) days of the mailing of the notice." s 2.29.1(C)(4): continuance "is not available for
-- applicants". Days run from the mailing of the notice.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the right to a hearing` MEANS
    PARTY `the recipient`
    MAY   `request a hearing`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the right to a hearing with continued benefits` MEANS
    PARTY `the recipient`
    MAY   `request a hearing and continued benefits`
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- s 2.29.3(A): "If a request for a hearing is made within the ten (10) day advance notice period, no action for reduction,
-- suspension, or discontinuance is taken until the hearing decision is issued except ... (1) When the reduction ... is
-- caused by a change in either State or Federal law that requires automatic grant adjustment for classes of recipients."
-- "However, a hearing is granted and the payment is continued when the reason for the appeal is incorrect grant
-- computation."
GIVEN `is a recipient, not an applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days after the notice was mailed that the hearing was requested` IS A NUMBER
      `the action is caused by a change in State or Federal law adjusting grants for a class of recipients` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is about incorrect grant computation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `benefits continue until the hearing decision` IF
        `is a recipient, not an applicant`
    AND `days after the notice was mailed that the hearing was requested` AT MOST 10
    AND (   (NOT `the action is caused by a change in State or Federal law adjusting grants for a class of recipients`)
         OR `the appeal is about incorrect grant computation`)
